<title>USA: Cooper Industries converts debentures.</title>
<headline>Cooper Industries converts debentures.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cooper Industries Inc said Wednesday it had converted into common shares 87 percent of the $190 million worth of debentures that were called last month.</p>
<p>Cooper, an electrical products manufacturer, said it had converted $165.4 million into shares and planned to redeem for cash the remaining 13 percent or $24.6 million on February 21.</p>
<p>On January 22, it called for a partial redemption of its 7.05-percent convertible subordinated debentures due 2015, which totalled $690 million.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
